From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: let platform data describe up to 32 ports

A switch probed through platform data (no device tree, as on x86
boards) can only name DSA_MAX_PORTS ports, 12 today. The BCM53314 of
the FortiGate 100D has 25 ports (CPU management port 0, ports 1-24),
of which 19 front ports and the CPU link are to be described, at their
hardware indexes. Raise the limit to 32, the number of addresses of an
MDIO bus, which DSA already uses to find the PHY of a user port.

Only the size of the arrays of struct dsa_chip_data changes; drivers
that size their own tables with DSA_MAX_PORTS (b53, bcm_sf2, ksz,
mv88e6xxx) are not built for the x86/fortigate subtarget.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/include/linux/platform_data/dsa.h
+++ b/include/linux/platform_data/dsa.h
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 struct net_device;
 
 #define DSA_MAX_SWITCHES	4
-#define DSA_MAX_PORTS		12
+#define DSA_MAX_PORTS		32
 #define DSA_RTABLE_NONE		-1
 
 struct dsa_chip_data {
